    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d190">

                <pb facs="0188" n="138" xml:id="pg138"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 811.142/4172b</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Consul at Archangel</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Cole</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-08-02T16:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 2, 1918,
                                4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Red Cross planning to send about 4,000 tons of medicines and supplied to
                    Archangel this month for distribution by Red Cross mission. Can ship enter
                    Archangel safely and what prospect of bringing flax as return cargo? Answer
                    urgent</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Polk</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
